<title>INDIA: Bank of India sets up convertibility panel.</title>
<headline>Bank of India sets up convertibility panel.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-run Bank of India has set up its own panel to study an official report charting a road map to make the rupee fully convertible on the capital account, a top official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have asked three of our officers to go into the report and study its import (substance) and impact,&quot; Bank of India general manager R. Nagarajan told Reuters.</p>
<p>The report on capital convertibility was submitted to the Reserve Bank of India earlier this month.</p>
<p>It set conditions and reforms needed to make the rupee fully convertible on the capital account by 2000.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
